---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Persistence Theory | CC0"
	description="This website and repository are offered under CC0 to encourage unrestricted reuse, remixing, adoption, and exploration."
>
	<section class="hero">
		<div class="hero-copy">
			<span class="eyebrow">CC0</span>
			<h1>Take the insights. No strings attached.</h1>
			<p>
				This project is released under <strong>CC0 1.0</strong> so people can explore,
				reuse, remix, translate, quote, fork, and build on the work without needing
				to negotiate permissions first.
			</p>

			<div class="button-row">
				<a class="button primary" href="/library">Browse the library</a>
				<a class="button" href="https://github.com/andrewmureddu/persistence-theory/blob/main/LICENSE">Read the full license</a>
			</div>
		</div>

		<aside class="hero-panel">
			<h2>Plain-language intent</h2>
			<p>
				The point is not just legal openness. It is to make the ideas portable. If
				something here is useful, take it into your own framework, your own project,
				your own vocabulary, and keep going.
			</p>
			<div class="dense">
				<div>
					<strong>You can</strong>
					<p>Reuse, adapt, republish, translate, excerpt, commercialize, and build on it.</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<strong>You do not need</strong>
					<p>Special permission, bespoke licensing, or a closed loop back to the project.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</aside>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="section-head">
			<span class="section-kicker">Why this matters</span>
			<h2 class="section-title">The site should invite adoption, not caution.</h2>
		</div>

		<div class="pillars">
			<article class="callout">
				<strong>For readers</strong>
				<p>
					If a proof, reduction, phrase, or conceptual frame helps you think, you can
					use it immediately.
				</p>
			</article>

			<article class="callout">
				<strong>For builders</strong>
				<p>
					If you want to adapt the ideas into software, research, writing, curriculum,
					or a different theory architecture, CC0 is there to remove friction.
				</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
